window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-kiryuin-fuuka"]=[{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v2-p278-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"kiriyama-ikuto ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka kiryuin takes the bench she s been sitting on the bench the whole time  kiriyama begs off  she addresses ayanokoji directly   kiriyama  can you not hear me   speak of the devil   fufu  you re with an interesting underclassman  so i said hello   ayanokouji       kiyotaka  right  i heard you became famous after a perfect score on a difficult math test   what are you doing  ayanokouji  we re leaving   you won t get anything from being with a guy like that  you know   staying with you is meaningless   ayanokouji s the one who should decide that  right  kiriyama  can t you leave any quicker   would you like to join me in a meaningful conversation   don t praise me like that  i m getting embarrassed   she s a lot like kouenji from your year  all her words and actions  if you take her seriously  you ll just be wasting your time   she s just a good student  but kiryuuin doesn t have anyone supporting her  unlike nagumo  she doesn t even have a single friend   thanks for the compliments  kiriyama   if you want to say something  say it quickly   it s enough as long as i can figure out what sort of person you are   being interested and cooperating are 2 completely different things  aren t they  there are some interesting people in my class  and sometimes i want to have a friendly conversation with them  just like what i m doing with you now   i m not interested in the system of aiming for class a of this school  although the biggest selling point of the school is that you can go to whatever university you want and find employment wherever you want  i believe i can achieve whatever i want with my own abilities  i simply chose to come to this school on a whim   would you have chosen this place if you knew before you came here that the structure of this school is centered around cooperation   that s not the case  i like this school  in fact  i haven t had a single complaint about life here since i arrived  the point system is also very pleasant   it seems that       you are fine with being hated by others   other people s       evaluations don t matter to me   i wanted to ask you something  but instead you re the one asking the questions   it s about time you told me about yourself   why me  there are many students who excel in their studies   are you planning to get first place in the uninhabited island exam   there s no student who doesn t want to be first  except maybe  for people       like you  kiryuuin senpai   letting aside first place  i m also one of the people who is aiming for a top spot  if i get a high position  i can get private points  i m the type to spend whatever i have  so i m always short of money   nagumo and kiriyama will obviously aim for 1st place  and it seems that there are some competent underclassmen  right  the upcoming special exam will determine the top student at the school   whether my interest in you disappears or not  it all depends on what you do in the uninhabited island exam   i see  you say some interesting things  underclassman  i m looking forward to fighting you  ayanokouji  her academic and physical abilities are both a    the only a a  in the school  her one weakness is adaptability  d  kouenji like self possession  faintly flirtatious needling  genuinely curious  no interest in class or system  only in her own excellence and in spending money  she sizes him up as the interesting underclassman  she mocks him openly  he cannot counter  next scene  she toys with him and declines his offer to help","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v2-p278-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Kiryūin takes the bench<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.278–285<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She&#x27;s been sitting on the bench the whole time; Kiriyama begs off; she addresses Ayanokōji directly.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Kiriyama. Can you not hear me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.278<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> “Speak of the devil…”<span class=\"pg\">p.278<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Fufu. You’re with an interesting underclassman, so I said hello.”<span class=\"pg\">p.278<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>32 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji …  …  Kiyotaka, right? I heard you became famous after a perfect score on a difficult math test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you doing, Ayanokouji? We’re leaving.”<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You won’t get anything from being with a guy like that, you know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Staying with you is meaningless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji’s the one who should decide that, right? Kiriyama, can’t you leave any quicker?”<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Would you like to join me in a meaningful conversation?”<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t praise me like that, I’m getting embarrassed!”<span class=\"pg\">p.280<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She’s a lot like Kouenji from your year. All her words and actions, if you take her seriously, you’ll just be wasting your time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.280<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She’s just a good student, but Kiryuuin doesn’t have anyone supporting her, unlike Nagumo. She doesn’t even have a single friend.”<span class=\"pg\">p.280<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thanks for the compliments, Kiriyama.”<span class=\"pg\">p.281<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you want to say something, say it quickly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.282<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s enough as long as I can figure out what sort of person you are.”<span class=\"pg\">p.283<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Being interested and cooperating are 2 completely different things, aren’t they? There are some interesting people in my class, and sometimes I want to have a friendly conversation with them, just like what I’m doing with you now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.283<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not interested in the system of aiming for Class A of this school. Although the biggest selling point of the school is that you can go to whatever university you want and find employment wherever you want, I believe I can achieve whatever I want with my own abilities. I simply chose to come to this school on a whim.”<span class=\"pg\">p.283<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Would you have chosen this place if you knew before you came here that the structure of this school is centered around cooperation?”<span class=\"pg\">p.283<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not the case. I like this school. In fact, I haven’t had a single complaint about life here since I arrived. The point system is also very pleasant.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems that …  …  you are fine with being hated by others.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Other people’s …  …  evaluations don’t matter to me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wanted to ask you something, but instead you’re the one asking the questions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s about time you told me about yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why me? There are many students who excel in their studies.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you planning to get first place in the uninhabited island exam?”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no student who doesn’t want to be first. Except maybe, for people …  …  like you, Kiryuuin-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Letting aside first place, I’m also one of the people who is aiming for a top spot. If I get a high position, I can get private points. I’m the type to spend whatever I have, so I’m always short of money.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nagumo and Kiriyama will obviously aim for 1st place, and it seems that there are some competent underclassmen, right? The upcoming special exam will determine the top student at the school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whether my interest in you disappears or not, it all depends on what you do in the uninhabited island exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.284<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. You say some interesting things, underclassman. I’m looking forward to fighting you, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.285<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her Academic and Physical Abilities are both A+ — the only A+/A+ in the school; her one weakness is Adaptability (D).<span class=\"pg\">p.280–285<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Kouenji-like self-possession; faintly flirtatious needling; genuinely curious; no interest in class or system, only in her own excellence and in spending money.<span class=\"pg\">p.278–285<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She sizes him up as the interesting underclassman.<span class=\"pg\">p.278–285<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> She mocks him openly; he cannot counter.<span class=\"pg\">p.278–285<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Next scene: she toys with him and declines his offer to help.<span class=\"pg\">p.286–292<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v2-p286-1\">→ After: Alone with Nagumo<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v2-p286-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"kiriyama-ikuto nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka alone with nagumo after ayanokoji leaves  her day resumes  the swaying blonde hair appears  followed by kiriyama   hey hey  the loyal dog came back with his master eh   if you re getting mad at this  then that means that you know what i m talking about  right now  no one should know who s the loyal dog and who s the owner  as i don t remember declaring who was who  i m simply stating from the perspective of an outsider who doesn t know anything  why  because the one who left and as returned is you  kiriyama  and so that fits the image of a loyal dog   this woman s a real pain in the ass   you ve got a dirty mouth  kiriyama  it doesn t suit the image of a serious vice president   agreed  so can the two of you disappear from my sight right now  it s a       waste of my precious time   a beloved comrade  you didn t say that with any sort of emotion at all   that s just your imagination   well  what does the student council president want from me  i thought i d never see you again   you re beautiful but charmless  and i don t have much interest in charmless women   i have charm  it s just that i haven t met a man who could draw it out yet   me too  but putting aside your personal tastes  why aren t i popular   if there s a man who can bring out the charming side of you  i d like to meet him   women with too high an ability are hard to deal with  unfortunately  i don t like those types either   i see  if that s the case then i ll never be able to meet your standards  if being too excellent is the reason why i haven t found a boyfriend  then i understand   i heard something from kiriyama  i would have never thought that someone who wasn t interested in both horikita senpai or i  would be interested in ayanokouji  i was surprised when i heard that   if possible  i too don t want to stay here for longer than i have to   someone who has never been with a man before  can understand the fundamentals of love   it s true that i ve never been in a relationship  but that s nothing to be ashamed of  rather  i should say that it has raised my value   like always  your way of thinking is rather strange   so  ayanokouji  is he someone worth keeping an eye on   there s a saying  that a predator doesn t reveal his fangs  right  he seems to have gotten a perfect score in a difficult test   there are people who hate being in the limelight and hide their talents  i ve defeated all of them  and they weren t very interesting   i have given you several chances to prove that  but till now you haven t done anything  and as a result ended up in class b   the moment you lose  you ll lose something immeasurable  student council president  however  it seems you ve misunderstood something  student council president  i m not underestimating you  i don t have the leadership skills that you or horikita manabu possessed  i m no good at making friends either  in fact i ve never had someone who i could consider a friend  let alone a close one  you know that  right   however  if we re talking about the other elements  it s different   well well  can you really say that there s definitely nothing in which you re inferior to me at   certainly  if you only look at the results  i failed miserably   you wanted some answers about ayanokouji  didn t you   interesting  i think his personality is far from it   you seem to be bored ever since horikita manabu left  so this underclassmen should be a good playmate for you  eh  if you re really serious  then you ll definitely get 1st place in the upcoming exam   of course i ll get 1st place  or maybe it ll be kiriyama  who s been dying to fight me  but to get control of the whole podium  i still need more groups  right  i ll give you this role  kiryuuin  if necessary  i ll even help you find comrades   i see  so you came here to ask for my help   the top 50  is enough for me  sorry that you had to come all this way for nothing   with that logic  nobody can give you any advice   then listen as if this were a monologue  you should look at what s going on in front of you  instead of playing with your underclassmen  if you pay too much attention to those behind you  you ll get badly hurt  her eval  a  a  d in adaptability  c  social  nagumo needs comrades on the podium  she takes top 50  and declines the whole offer  sharp  self sufficient  entirely unbothered  she wins by surviving  not by commanding  nagumo s wanted something she never agreed to give  she treats him as a rival who bore her  she tells him to his face he s a loyal dog  she keeps him on hold","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v2-p286-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Alone with Nagumo<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.286–292<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After Ayanokōji leaves; her day resumes; the swaying blonde hair appears, followed by Kiriyama.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hey hey, the loyal dog came back with his master eh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.286<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If you’re getting mad at this, then that means that you know what I’m talking about. Right now, no one should know who’s the loyal dog and who’s the owner, as I don’t remember declaring who was who. I’m simply stating from the…”<span class=\"pg\">p.286<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> “This woman’s a real pain in the ass…”<span class=\"pg\">p.286<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>38 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you’re getting mad at this, then that means that you know what I’m talking about. Right now, no one should know who’s the loyal dog and who’s the owner, as I don’t remember declaring who was who. I’m simply stating from the perspective of an outsider who doesn’t know anything. Why? Because the one who left and as returned is you, Kiriyama, and so that fits the image of a loyal dog.”<span class=\"pg\">p.286<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve got a dirty mouth, Kiriyama, it doesn’t suit the image of a serious vice president.”<span class=\"pg\">p.286<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Agreed. So can the two of you disappear from my sight right now? It’s a …  …  waste of my precious time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.286<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A beloved comrade? You didn’t say that with any sort of emotion at all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s just your imagination.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well. What does the student council president want from me? I thought I’d never see you again.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re beautiful but charmless, and I don’t have much interest in charmless women.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have charm. It’s just that I haven’t met a man who could draw it out yet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Me too. But putting aside your personal tastes, why aren’t I popular?”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If there’s a man who can bring out the charming side of you, I’d like to meet him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Women with too high an ability are hard to deal with. Unfortunately, I don’t like those types either.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see, if that’s the case then I’ll never be able to meet your standards. If being too excellent is the reason why I haven’t found a boyfriend, then I understand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I heard something from Kiriyama. I would have never thought that someone who wasn’t interested in both Horikita-senpai or I, would be interested in Ayanokouji. I was surprised when I heard that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.288<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If possible, I too don’t want to stay here for longer than I have to.”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Someone who has never been with a man before, can understand the fundamentals of love?”<span class=\"pg\">p.288<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s true that I’ve never been in a relationship, but that’s nothing to be ashamed of. Rather, I should say that it has raised my value?”<span class=\"pg\">p.288<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Like always, your way of thinking is rather strange.”<span class=\"pg\">p.288<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So… Ayanokouji? Is he someone worth keeping an eye on?”<span class=\"pg\">p.288<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s a saying, that a predator doesn’t reveal his fangs, right? He seems to have gotten a perfect score in a difficult test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There are people who hate being in the limelight and hide their talents. I’ve defeated all of them, and they weren’t very interesting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have given you several chances to prove that, but till now you haven’t done anything, and as a result ended up in Class B.”<span class=\"pg\">p.290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The moment you lose, you’ll lose something immeasurable, student council president. However, it seems you’ve misunderstood something, student council president. I’m not underestimating you. I don’t have the leadership skills that you or Horikita Manabu possessed. I’m no good at making friends either, in fact I’ve never had someone who I could consider a friend, let alone a close one. You know that, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, if we’re talking about the other elements, it’s different.”<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well well, can you really say that there’s definitely nothing in which you’re inferior to me at?”<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Certainly, if you only look at the results, I failed miserably.”<span class=\"pg\">p.290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You wanted some answers about Ayanokouji, didn’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Interesting? I think his personality is far from it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You seem to be bored ever since Horikita Manabu left. So this underclassmen should be a good playmate for you, eh? If you’re really serious, then you’ll definitely get 1st place in the upcoming exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course I’ll get 1st place. Or maybe it’ll be Kiriyama, who’s been dying to fight me. But to get control of the whole podium, I still need more groups, right? I’ll give you this role, Kiryuuin. If necessary, I’ll even help you find comrades.”<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. So you came here to ask for my help?”<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The top 50% is enough for me. Sorry that you had to come all this way for nothing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “With that logic, nobody can give you any advice”<span class=\"pg\">p.292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then listen as if this were a monologue. You should look at what’s going on in front of you, instead of playing with your underclassmen. If you pay too much attention to those behind you, you’ll get badly hurt.”<span class=\"pg\">p.292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her eval: A+ A+, D in adaptability, C+ social; Nagumo needs comrades on the podium; she takes top-50% and declines the whole offer.<span class=\"pg\">p.286–292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sharp, self-sufficient, entirely unbothered; she wins by surviving, not by commanding; Nagumo&#x27;s wanted something she never agreed to give.<span class=\"pg\">p.286–292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> She treats him as a rival who bore her.<span class=\"pg\">p.286–292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> She tells him to his face he&#x27;s a loyal dog.<span class=\"pg\">p.286–292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She keeps him on hold.<span class=\"pg\">p.285–292<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v2-p278-1\">← Before: Kiryūin takes the bench<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v3-p50-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka kiryuin senpai  a fellow solo third year spotted among the calm class 3 b students disembarking  approaches ayanokoji at the starting area while he searches for nagumo   you re still here  ayanokoji   but you re alone  right  you should be fine to think it over while you walk   if there s something you wanna know  i can help explain it to you   there s something  enchanting about seeing the entire student body scatter throughout the uninhabited island   though there are more than 400 of us  we re nothing but insignificant specks of dust in comparison   hoh  sounds like we ve got the same destination then  at least for this first one   please don t be too hard on me  then  a third year  class 3 b  who also chose to tackle the exam alone   keen eyed  questions why he lingers  calm  even wistful  enchanting   insignificant specks of dust  and seemingly looking forward to the exam  shares his d7 destination and proposes traveling together  recognizes him  offers help  then travels with him toward d7","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v3-p50-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Kiryūin-senpai, a fellow solo third-year<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.50–52<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Spotted among the calm Class 3-B students disembarking; approaches Ayanokōji at the starting area while he searches for Nagumo.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You&#x27;re still here, Ayanokōji?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;But you&#x27;re alone, right? You should be fine to think it over while you walk.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If there&#x27;s something you wanna know, I can help explain it to you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There&#x27;s something… enchanting about seeing the entire student body scatter throughout the uninhabited island.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Though there are more than 400 of us, we&#x27;re nothing but insignificant specks of dust in comparison.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hoh? Sounds like we&#x27;ve got the same destination then. At least for this first one.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Please don&#x27;t be too hard on me, then.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> A third-year (Class 3-B) who also chose to tackle the exam alone — keen-eyed (questions why he lingers), calm, even wistful (&quot;enchanting,&quot; &quot;insignificant specks of dust&quot;), and seemingly looking forward to the exam; shares his D7 destination and proposes traveling together.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Recognizes him; offers help, then travels with him toward D7.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v4-p81-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi shiba-katsunori tsukishiro kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 3  overlook greeting  the nagumo game on day nine at the designated area arrival he walks up to her at the overlook  she has jumped from 11th or lower to 9th this morning  she debriefs him on the field   you have arrived quite late  ayanokouji   it looks like it is   i thought i had a tough competitor for the reward in order of arrival  but was it you   i don t know what s up with that  it s not uncommon for there to be different tables in the same area  more than that  i thought that kiryuuin senpai was not interested in the top ten groups   this uninhabited island test was more fun than i thought it would be  and i was thrilled beyond my age   i m going to continue with my current rhythm for a while longer   shouldn t you be aiming for number one   everyone is competing with each other for the podium  i could not continue with that game  however  if miyabi nagumo collapses down  the story could be a little different   do you think nagumo is going to release kouenji as he is right now   in such a state of conflict and struggle  nor can i say that nagumo will ever win  sure you have been watching everything up to now  but the time has come for you to move your chips  depending on how things go  we could see a period where neither team scores   because hitting your opponent is an important part of a battle   don t you aspire to move to the top   i m sorry  but i don t see how can i be in the top ten   i see  i thought you would have scored almost as many points as i did   several groups will soon lose their performance  we just have to keep trying and not give up   all i can say is that you can t let your guard down  not even for a moment   yesterday i went through the starting point to obtain information  it seems that groups that have started to suffer from food and water shortages are trying to get ahead by separating some of their members to avoid joint collapse   it is a wise decision   i am sure that the last 10 will have some hope  no matter which group will withdraw  a man who has lost his way will use whatever means at his disposal  stay alert  okay   shouldn t it be something a woman  kiryuuin senpai  should be worried about   hmm  it s true that  as a pretty and merciful maiden  i might also feel a sense of danger   well if it comes to that   i would just have to force it out   so that s a  no  i dare you to go there and see for yourself  enjoys the game  watches from the third year leaderboard  reads the koenji nagumo stalemate as a deadlocked chess match  teases him about  a pretty and merciful maiden  and implies she might force it out  she lets him have the first trip to the bonus pool  sizes him up as a genuine competitor  he lies about not aspiring to the top ten  expects the koenji nagumo game to split at some point  appears during the 2 on 1 fight   had watched from behind a tree  deliberately broke her watch so her gps wouldn t show her approach   i wonder what the acting director and the classroom teacher do with a student in such a deserted place   actually  i ve been watching you from behind the big tree for a while  but i couldn t take the two on one situation   of course  as your senpai  shouldn t it be normal for me to protect my kouhai   i ll tell you  i ll hold them for a minute or two at least   keep your fists up and try to create an atmosphere of tension   i am a lady  what do you think    on whether she s hit anyone playful and bold   breaks her own watch to sneak up  appears to protect her  kouhai  holds shiba  a  ridiculous level  fighter  through defense alone  and teases ayanokoji into a fighting pose  afterward exhausted but proud  intervenes on his behalf  calls him  kouhai  and helps him win  holds him off while ayanokoji fights tsukishiro  confronts the acting director over fighting a student in a deserted place","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v4-p81-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: Overlook greeting; the Nagumo game<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.81–85<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On day nine at the designated-area arrival he walks up to her at the overlook; she has jumped from 11th or lower to 9th this morning; she debriefs him on the field. Appears during the 2-on-1 fight — had watched from behind a tree, deliberately broke her watch so her GPS wouldn&#x27;t show her approach.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"shiba-katsunori.html\">Shiba Katsunori<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You have arrived quite late, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “It looks like it is”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I thought I had a tough competitor for the reward in order of arrival, but was it you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>33 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know what’s up with that. It’s not uncommon for there to be different tables in the same area. More than that, I thought that Kiryuuin-senpai was not interested in the top ten groups.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This uninhabited island test was more fun than I thought it would be, and I was thrilled beyond my age.”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m going to continue with my current rhythm for a while longer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Shouldn’t you be aiming for number one?”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Everyone is competing with each other for the podium. I could not continue with that game. However, if Miyabi Nagumo collapses down, the story could be a little different.”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you think Nagumo is going to release Kouenji as he is right now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In such a state of conflict and struggle, Nor can I say that Nagumo will ever win. Sure you have been watching everything up to now, but the time has come for you to move your chips. Depending on how things go, we could see a period where neither team scores.”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because hitting your opponent is an important part of a battle.”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you aspire to move to the top?”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, but I don’t see how can I be in the top ten.”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. I thought you would have scored almost as many points as I did.”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Several groups will soon lose their performance. We just have to keep trying and not give up.”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “All I can say is that you can’t let your guard down, not even for a moment.”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yesterday I went through the starting point to obtain information. It seems that groups that have started to suffer from food and water shortages are trying to get ahead by separating some of their members to avoid joint collapse.”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It is a wise decision.”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I am sure that the last 10 will have some hope, no matter which group will withdraw. A man who has lost his way will use whatever means at his disposal. Stay alert, okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Shouldn’t it be something a woman, Kiryuuin-senpai, should be worried about?”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm… It’s true that, as a pretty and merciful maiden, I might also feel a sense of danger”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well if it comes to that ......., I would just have to force it out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So that’s a.... no, I dare you to go there and see for yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Enjoys the game, watches from the third-year leaderboard, reads the Kōenji–Nagumo stalemate as a deadlocked chess match; teases him about “a pretty and merciful maiden” and implies she might force it out; she lets him have the first trip to the bonus pool.<span class=\"pg\">p.81–85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Sizes him up as a genuine competitor; he lies about not aspiring to the top ten.<span class=\"pg\">p.81–85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Expects the Kōenji–Nagumo game to split at some point.<span class=\"pg\">p.83–84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wonder what the Acting Director and the classroom teacher do with a student in such a deserted place.”<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Actually, I&#x27;ve been watching you from behind the big tree for a while, but I couldn&#x27;t take the two-on-one situation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. As your senpai, shouldn&#x27;t it be normal for me to protect my kouhai?”<span class=\"pg\">p.263<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I&#x27;ll tell you. I&#x27;ll hold them for a minute or two at least.”<span class=\"pg\">p.263<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Keep your fists up and try to create an atmosphere of tension.”<span class=\"pg\">p.263<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I am a lady. What do you think?” — on whether she&#x27;s hit anyone<span class=\"pg\">p.264<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Playful and bold — breaks her own watch to sneak up, appears to protect her “kouhai,” holds Shiba (a “ridiculous level” fighter) through defense alone, and teases Ayanokōji into a fighting pose; afterward exhausted but proud.<span class=\"pg\">p.261–273<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Intervenes on his behalf, calls him “kouhai,” and helps him win.<span class=\"pg\">p.261–272<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiba Katsunori<\/b> Holds him off while Ayanokōji fights Tsukishiro.<span class=\"pg\">p.263–270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Confronts the acting director over fighting a student in a deserted place.<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v4_5-p38-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kiriyama nagumo-miyabi kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka kiryuin at the pool  teasing ayanokoji and kiriyama  looks like you might be in trouble  ayanokoji   it looks like quite the frightening strategy to me   as expected of the student council president  he s played a bizarre  yet effective card against this flawless person in front of me   we re comrades that have been through the line of fire together  so i know that your abilities are limitless  right   to nagumo  you should ve been nothing more than a toy   i can tell that he s the type of person you re no good at dealing with  am i right   i m sorry  but i can t help you with this one   if there were a retention system at this school  i might ve considered it   ayanokoji and i are in a romantic relationship   fufu  it s a joke kiriyama  relaxed on a deck chair in sunglasses  she reads the third years  surveillance and nagumo s strategy clearly  praises ayanokoji s  limitless  ability  they re  comrades  from i2  declines to help  wants a quiet life  almost wishes she could repeat a year  and deliberately needles the deadpan kiriyama   even joking that she and ayanokoji are  in a romantic relationship  teases and accurately reads him  they re  comrades  from the i2 incident  needles the irritable vice president  he tries to escape her  understands his strategy and character well","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v4_5-p38-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Kiryūin at the pool: teasing Ayanokōji and Kiriyama<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.38–45<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"kiriyama.html\">Kiriyama<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Looks like you might be in trouble, Ayanokōji.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It looks like quite the frightening strategy to me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;As expected of the Student Council President. He&#x27;s played a bizarre, yet effective card against this flawless person in front of me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We&#x27;re comrades that have been through the line of fire together, so I know that your abilities are limitless, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;To Nagumo, you should&#x27;ve been nothing more than a toy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I can tell that he&#x27;s the type of person you&#x27;re no good at dealing with. Am I right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m sorry, but I can&#x27;t help you with this one.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If there were a retention system at this school, I might&#x27;ve considered it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokōji and I are in a romantic relationship.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Fufu, it&#x27;s a joke Kiriyama.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Relaxed on a deck chair in sunglasses, she reads the third-years&#x27; surveillance and Nagumo&#x27;s strategy clearly, praises Ayanokōji&#x27;s &quot;limitless&quot; ability (they&#x27;re &quot;comrades&quot; from I2), declines to help (wants a quiet life, almost wishes she could repeat a year), and deliberately needles the deadpan Kiriyama — even joking that she and Ayanokōji are &quot;in a romantic relationship.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.38–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Teases and accurately reads him; they&#x27;re &quot;comrades&quot; from the I2 incident.<span class=\"pg\">p.38–44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama<\/b> Needles the irritable vice president; he tries to escape her.<span class=\"pg\">p.43–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Understands his strategy and character well.<span class=\"pg\">p.41–43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v4_5-p155-1\">→ After: Mentions: the type of person he&#x27;s no good at<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v4_5-p155-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"","w":"kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka mentions  the type of person he s no good at ayanokoji recalls kiryuin s words  nagumo might be  the type of person i would be no good at dealing with    her assessment on p 42","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v4_5-p155-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Mentions: the type of person he&#x27;s no good at<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.155<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Ayanokōji recalls Kiryūin&#x27;s words: Nagumo might be &quot;the type of person I would be no good at dealing with&quot; — her assessment on p.42.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v4_5-p38-1\">← Before: Kiryūin at the pool: teasing Ayanokōji and Kiriyama<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v4_5-p289-1\">→ After: Short story: &quot;When You are the Older One&quot; — the stares at the pool<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v4_5-p289-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka short story   when you are the older one    the stares at the pool from her own pov  relaxing by the pool in sunglasses  notices the third years all look at ayanokoji in unison  curious  she calls out to him  her  off mode  switch flips on   spending a holiday like this just relaxing ain t bad from time to time   i see  so that s what s going on   looks like you re in for some trouble  ayanokouji   i m talking about the 3rd year students  there s no way you haven t noticed them  am i right   so you did notice after all  relaxed but sharp   reads nagumo s surveillance of ayanokoji at once  notes he s only pretending not to notice  and is fascinated by him  ayanokoji is seriously an interesting man  wishes  wistfully  that they were the same age so she could observe him for another year   a feeling forming  within me  finds him interesting  teases him about the stares and senses nagumo is taking him seriously  her fellow third year  his involvement means  trouble is brewing","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v4_5-p289-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Short story: &quot;When You are the Older One&quot; — the stares at the pool<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.289–290<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">From her own POV, relaxing by the pool in sunglasses, notices the third-years all look at Ayanokōji in unison; curious, she calls out to him (her &quot;OFF-mode&quot; switch flips ON).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;Spending a holiday like this just relaxing ain&#x27;t bad from time to time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;I see… so that&#x27;s what&#x27;s going on.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;Looks like you&#x27;re in for some trouble, Ayanokouji.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m talking about the 3rd year students. There&#x27;s no way you haven&#x27;t noticed them, am I right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;So you did notice after all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Relaxed but sharp — reads Nagumo&#x27;s surveillance of Ayanokōji at once, notes he&#x27;s only pretending not to notice, and is fascinated by him (Ayanokōji is seriously an interesting man); wishes, wistfully, that they were the same age so she could observe him for another year — a feeling forming &quot;within me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.289–290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Finds him interesting; teases him about the stares and senses Nagumo is taking him seriously.<span class=\"pg\">p.289–290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Her fellow third-year; his involvement means &quot;trouble is brewing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.290<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v4_5-p155-1\">← Before: Mentions: the type of person he&#x27;s no good at<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v6-p252-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"action spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 5  the probe at the ribbon   she needles nagumo  nagumo pov  between her events at the sports festival she drifts to where nagumo is catching his breath after his fifth consecutive win  she asks him about his lineup and his motives  he does not turn  she needles him for show   poor little thing  how about i take you on   fufufu  you got me  huh   you should stop giving these underclassmen the time of day  you ve already dominated our grade and are fixed at class a  on top of that  you ve achieved a lot as the student council president  that should be enough  i recommend you graduate quietly  her taunt lands as casual surface   she does not turn to his face either  the challenge is polite by both  the lines follow the printed alternation with nagumo s answers   don t make me laugh  as if winning a competition of that level would mean anything to me  is nagumo s opening answer  recorded in nagumo s own record  the narration  almost as if she was advising him on what to do  kiryuin senpai admonished him    the translation does not tag speech directly on that line    not quoted here as her speech  her rival in rank and graduation trajectory  the tournament counts the fifth consecutive win of the other  their shared ground is zero","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v6-p252-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: The probe at the ribbon — she needles Nagumo (Nagumo-POV)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.252–253<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Between her events at the Sports Festival she drifts to where Nagumo is catching his breath after his fifth consecutive win; she asks him about his lineup and his motives; he does not turn; she needles him for show.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Poor little thing, how about I take you on?”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Fufufu. You got me, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You should stop giving these underclassmen the time of day. You&#x27;ve already dominated our grade and are fixed at Class A. On top of that, you&#x27;ve achieved a lot as the student council president. That should be enough. I recommend…”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You should stop giving these underclassmen the time of day. You&#x27;ve already dominated our grade and are fixed at Class A. On top of that, you&#x27;ve achieved a lot as the student council president. That should be enough. I recommend you graduate quietly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Her taunt lands as casual surface — she does not turn to his face either; the challenge is polite by both.<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The lines follow the printed alternation with Nagumo’s answers; “Don’t make me laugh. As if winning a competition of that level would mean anything to me.” is Nagumo’s opening answer, recorded in Nagumo’s own record; the narration (“Almost as if she was advising him on what to do, Kiryuin-senpai admonished him.” — the translation does not tag speech directly on that line) — not quoted here as her speech.<span class=\"pg\">p.252–253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Her rival in rank and graduation trajectory; the tournament counts the fifth consecutive win of the other; their shared ground is zero.<span class=\"pg\">p.252–253<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v7-p39-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka named in nagumo s rival analysis  at times  there may have been people around him who were as talented as him  such as kiryuin  but if they didn t try to catch up and overtake nagumo  they    were no different than weeds and pebbles on the side of the road    the narration on nagumo s opponents  she was named in nagumo s never loses analysis  nagumo considered her a peer who never tried to close the gap","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v7-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Named in Nagumo&#x27;s rival analysis<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.39<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “At times, there may have been people around him who were as talented as him, such as Kiryūin, but if they didn&#x27;t try to catch up and overtake Nagumo, they …  were no different than weeds and pebbles on the side of the road.” — the narration on Nagumo&#x27;s opponents.<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> She was named in Nagumo&#x27;s never-loses analysis; Nagumo considered her a peer who never tried to close the gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v7-p40-1\">→ After: Named in Nagumo&#x27;s rival analysis<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v7-p40-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"","w":"nagumo-miyabi kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka named in nagumo s rival analysis  at times  there may have been people around him who were as talented as him  such as kiryuin  but if they didn t try to catch up and overtake nagumo  they    were no different than weeds and pebbles on the side of the road    the narration on nagumo s opponents  one of the few talented students around nagumo who never tried to close the gap","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v7-p40-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Named in Nagumo&#x27;s rival analysis<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.40<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> “At times, there may have been people around him who were as talented as him, such as Kiryūin, but if they didn&#x27;t try to catch up and overtake Nagumo, they …  were no different than weeds and pebbles on the side of the road.” — the narration on Nagumo&#x27;s opponents.<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> One of the few talented students around Nagumo who never tried to close the gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v7-p39-1\">← Before: Named in Nagumo&#x27;s rival analysis<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v9-p29-1","v":"y2v9","y":2,"o":25,"k":"spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi kiriyama-ikuto ichinose-honami kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka kiryuin interrupts the election meeting she enters the student council room without knocking to press an appointment she says kiriyama made with her  and refuses nagumo s attempt to put her off   going so far as to put her foot on an empty chair   let me interrupt you  nagumo   i refuse  blunt  impatient and confrontational   she ignores protocol  refuses to wait quietly  and is undeterred by the president  she brushes off his demand that she wait  he calls her an unexpected guest  says he had agreed to make time for her  she lays out the accusation   that yamanaka  a third year class d student  tried to slip lipstick into her bag at keyaki mall and blamed nagumo   and offers to drop the matter if nagumo apologizes   you don t understand me well enough to say  it s not like me  unfortunately  i have a great dislike for acts like shoplifting   you can rest assured  if i can hear an apology from you  i promise you that this matter will be put to rest  unaware of ichinose s shoplifting past  she speaks bluntly about her hatred of the act  when nagumo refuses and walks away  she is stunned  her blunt talk of shoplifting darkens ichinose s expression   unknowingly striking a nerve","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v9-p29-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Kiryūin interrupts the election meeting<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9 · p.29–30<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She enters the student-council room without knocking to press an appointment she says Kiriyama made with her, and refuses Nagumo&#x27;s attempt to put her off — going so far as to put her foot on an empty chair. She lays out the accusation — that Yamanaka, a third-year Class D student, tried to slip lipstick into her bag at Keyaki Mall and blamed Nagumo — and offers to drop the matter if Nagumo apologizes.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Let me interrupt you, Nagumo.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I refuse.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You don&#x27;t understand me well enough to say &#x27;it&#x27;s not like me.&#x27; Unfortunately, I have a great dislike for acts like shoplifting.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Blunt, impatient and confrontational — she ignores protocol, refuses to wait quietly, and is undeterred by the president.<span class=\"pg\">p.29–30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> She brushes off his demand that she wait; he calls her an unexpected guest.<span class=\"pg\">p.29–30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> Says he had agreed to make time for her.<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You can rest assured. If I can hear an apology from you, I promise you that this matter will be put to rest.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Unaware of Ichinose&#x27;s shoplifting past, she speaks bluntly about her hatred of the act; when Nagumo refuses and walks away, she is stunned.<span class=\"pg\">p.31–32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Her blunt talk of shoplifting darkens Ichinose&#x27;s expression — unknowingly striking a nerve.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v9-p76-1\">→ After: Kiryūin recruits Ayanokōji to investigate<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v9-p76-1","v":"y2v9","y":2,"o":25,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka kiryuin recruits ayanokoji to investigate she stops ayanokoji outside the council room and asks him to dig into the shoplifting case   nagumo and kiriyama have blocked her from re questioning yamanaka  and she needs someone with a neutral perspective and fighting ability   can i have a moment of your time  ayanokouji   no  my pride won t allow me to meditate on his attempt to incriminate me   cooperate with me  i don t have anyone i can call a friend  i can t act like a detective  prideful but strategic   she refuses to let the frame up rest  flatters ayanokoji s abilities  and invokes his debt from the island exam to force his cooperation  presses him into investigating by appealing to his neutrality and fighting sense  blocked by him from re questioning yamanaka","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v9-p76-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Kiryūin recruits Ayanokōji to investigate<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9 · p.76–78<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She stops Ayanokōji outside the council room and asks him to dig into the shoplifting case — Nagumo and Kiriyama have blocked her from re-questioning Yamanaka, and she needs someone with a neutral perspective and fighting ability.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Can I have a moment of your time, Ayanokouji?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;No. My pride won&#x27;t allow me to meditate on his attempt to incriminate me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Cooperate with me. I don&#x27;t have anyone I can call a friend. I can&#x27;t act like a detective.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Prideful but strategic — she refuses to let the frame-up rest, flatters Ayanokōji&#x27;s abilities, and invokes his debt from the island exam to force his cooperation.<span class=\"pg\">p.76–78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Presses him into investigating by appealing to his neutrality and fighting sense.<span class=\"pg\">p.76–78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Blocked by him from re-questioning Yamanaka.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v9-p29-1\">← Before: Kiryūin interrupts the election meeting<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v9-p180-1\">→ After: Kiryūin: the shoplifting complaint and her demand for an apology<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v9-p180-1","v":"y2v9","y":2,"o":25,"k":"spoken","w":"kiriyama-ikuto nagumo-miyabi kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka kiryuin  the shoplifting complaint and her demand for an apology in the hearing she files a complaint over the attempt to frame her as a shoplifter  revealing that the third year yamanaka confessed she had been instructed   and naming nagumo as the alleged orderer   sorry to keep you waiting  new student council president   i just can t believe yamanaka acted out of personal resentment  she presses nagumo  spars with kiriyama  and rejects a quiet cover up  when kiriyama finally confesses he used her as the target  her sole demand is an apology from the real culprit   all i want is an apology from the real culprit  direct and principled   she refuses to let the matter be buried  wants the truth rather than a convenient story  and cares about the apology more than punishment  her classmate whom she suspected  he confesses he framed her deliberately  she names him as the one who allegedly ordered the framing  he denies it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v9-p180-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Kiryūin: the shoplifting complaint and her demand for an apology<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9 · p.180–190<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the hearing she files a complaint over the attempt to frame her as a shoplifter, revealing that the third-year Yamanaka confessed she had been instructed — and naming Nagumo as the alleged orderer. She presses Nagumo, spars with Kiriyama, and rejects a quiet cover-up; when Kiriyama finally confesses he used her as the target, her sole demand is an apology from the real culprit.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Sorry to keep you waiting, new student council president.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I just can&#x27;t believe Yamanaka acted out of personal resentment.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;All I want is an apology from the real culprit.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Direct and principled — she refuses to let the matter be buried, wants the truth rather than a convenient story, and cares about the apology more than punishment.<span class=\"pg\">p.180–190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> Her classmate whom she suspected; he confesses he framed her deliberately.<span class=\"pg\">p.189–190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> She names him as the one who allegedly ordered the framing; he denies it.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v9-p76-1\">← Before: Kiryūin recruits Ayanokōji to investigate<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v9_5-p45-1","v":"y2v9.5","y":2,"o":26,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 3  kiryuin at the mall  the yogurt maker exchange finds ayanokoji staring at the supermarket s dairy section  hunched over and bereft over the sold out yogurt maker from the keyaki mall sale  walks him out of his daze  laughs at his loss  advises buying online  shows him the same model at the same price as the sale  reveals she knew it wasn t a real sale  reveals she followed him only from curiosity about his unusual name  confesses that she once wanted to repeat a grade to keep watching him train  declines even 20 million private points to rush to class a  says private points can t buy everything  e g  she remarks she once tried to use points to fire the teachers she didn t like   no comment  reveals she was a grandchild raised by her ojii sama  ojou sama  at home  picked this school to escape being born into wealth  plans scholarship   part time to live a normal unremarkable life   like his  says nagumo is gathering rumors of second years for the third term  that the special exam ahead might be more troublesome than he thinks  her memory of last year s second term special exam is oddly vague  they part   before feeling down  try looking online  you might find it surprisingly cheap   if there was a system to repeat a grade in this school   this is just my intuition  but i have a feeling that we ll meet again somewhere  follows him to the mall  talks about privilege  class a and self funded lives  he listens but reveals nothing  mutual respect under the odds  her  failure  to join any class battle teams her with a person who genuinely doesn t care about rank","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v9_5-p45-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: Kiryūin at the mall; the yogurt-maker exchange<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9.5 · p.45–58<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Finds Ayanokōji staring at the supermarket&#x27;s dairy section, hunched-over and bereft over the sold-out yogurt maker from the Keyaki Mall sale; walks him out of his daze. Laughs at his loss, advises buying online; shows him the same model at the same price as the sale; reveals she knew it wasn&#x27;t a real sale; reveals she followed him only from curiosity about his unusual name. Confesses that she once wanted to repeat a grade to keep watching him train; declines even 20 million private points to rush to Class A; says private points can&#x27;t buy everything (e.g. she remarks she once tried to use points to fire the teachers she didn&#x27;t like — no-comment). Reveals she was a grandchild raised by her ojii-sama (&quot;ojou-sama&quot; at home); picked this school to escape being born into wealth; plans scholarship + part-time to live a normal unremarkable life — like his. Says Nagumo is gathering rumors of second-years for the third term, that the special exam ahead might be more troublesome than he thinks; her memory of last year&#x27;s second-term special exam is oddly vague; they part.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Before feeling down, try looking online. You might find it surprisingly cheap.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If there was a system to repeat a grade in this school.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;This is just my intuition, but I have a feeling that we&#x27;ll meet again somewhere.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Follows him to the mall, talks about privilege, Class A and self-funded lives; he listens but reveals nothing; mutual respect under the odds.<span class=\"pg\">p.45–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Her &quot;failure&quot; to join any class battle teams her with a person who genuinely doesn&#x27;t care about rank.<span class=\"pg\">p.45–58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p32-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamamura-miki morishita-ai hashimoto-masayoshi kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 1  the green tea brand class 3 b s kiryuin fuka stops by the beverage cooler  her shoulder lightly collides with yamamura s  she turns her gaze on kiyotaka like a beverage promoter   i like this brand s tea  you can feel the umami and aroma as if it were brewed in a teapot  right ayanokoji   oh  it s good to have a wide circle  you should cherish your friends   i ll remember all three of you  she knows him by name  aloof reputation among third years noted  their shoulders collide  she apologizes to her first  she learns yamamura and morishita are in class a  he introduces himself as class a  she lightly brushes off his offered hand","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: The green-tea brand<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.32–33<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 3-B&#x27;s Kiryūin Fūka stops by the beverage cooler; her shoulder lightly collides with Yamamura&#x27;s; she turns her gaze on Kiyotaka like a beverage promoter.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"yamamura-miki.html\">Yamamura Miki<\/a> · <a href=\"morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I like this brand&#x27;s tea. You can feel the umami and aroma as if it were brewed in a teapot, right Ayanokōji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Oh? It&#x27;s good to have a wide circle. You should cherish your friends.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I&#x27;ll remember all three of you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She knows him by name; aloof reputation among third-years noted.<span class=\"pg\">p.32–33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamamura Miki<\/b> Their shoulders collide; she apologizes to her first.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> She learns Yamamura and Morishita are in Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> He introduces himself as Class A; she lightly brushes off his offered hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p38-1\">→ After: Ch.2: The group 20 leader<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p38-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"","w":"kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 2  the group 20 leader the bus ride  kiryuin is named in the printout   i seem to be in group 20 with kiryuin senpai  at the end of the fifth page    his assignment  he reads all 20 groups  named in narration  not present on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p38-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: The group 20 leader<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.38<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The bus ride; Kiryūin is named in the printout.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “I seem to be in group 20 with Kiryūin-senpai, at the end of the fifth page.” — his assignment; he reads all 20 groups.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Named in narration; not present on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p32-1\">← Before: Ch.1: The green-tea brand<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p45-1\">→ After: Ch.2: Hands in her pockets<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p45-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 2  hands in her pockets after the highway stop  she waits with hands in her jersey jacket pockets as the leader of group 20  the first face he sees at the inn   i m counting on you   now that the greetings are over  let s have lunch  let s disband for now   then i ll leave it to you  she leaves hashimoto to run the lunch  she disappears into the inn alone  her list  16 first second years  kiyotaka is group 20  chosen by nagumo to watch the match  she gives him a lead the group offer","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p45-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: Hands in her pockets<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.45–52<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After the highway stop; she waits with hands in her jersey jacket pockets as the leader of Group 20; the first face he sees at the inn.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I&#x27;m counting on you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Now that the greetings are over, let&#x27;s have lunch. Let&#x27;s disband for now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Then I&#x27;ll leave it to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She leaves Hashimoto to run the lunch; she disappears into the inn alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her list: 16 first/second-years; Kiyotaka is Group 20.<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Chosen by Nagumo to watch the match; she gives him a lead-the-group offer.<span class=\"pg\">p.45–52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p38-1\">← Before: Ch.2: The group 20 leader<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p57-1\">→ After: Ch.2: The bet negotiation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p57-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"","w":"kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 2  the bet negotiation the break room  the bet is being set   you can clearly refuse if you don t like it  you know  even if you say you won t pay anything when you lose  the fact that you lost will remain    kiryuin s role in the negotiation  she is consulted by nagumo   you participate in all the games  and when you lose three times  that s your defeat    the terms  she knows in advance   of course  i ve told kiryuin that you re participating in all the games    her role in setting the stage  named in dialogue  not present on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p57-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: The bet negotiation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.57–59<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The break room; the bet is being set.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “You can clearly refuse if you don&#x27;t like it, you know? Even if you say you won&#x27;t pay anything when you lose, the fact that you lost will remain.” — Kiryūin&#x27;s role in the negotiation; she is consulted by Nagumo.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “You participate in all the games. And when you lose three times, that&#x27;s your defeat.” — the terms; she knows in advance.<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Of course, I&#x27;ve told Kiryūin that you&#x27;re participating in all the games.” — her role in setting the stage.<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Named in dialogue; not present on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–59<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p45-1\">← Before: Ch.2: Hands in her pockets<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p60-1\">→ After: Ch.2: She sniffed out the bet<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p60-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 2  she sniffed out the bet break room  she strolls in late  she already knows about the nagumo match and proposes handing over leader authority   i m sorry i m late  has the discussion been settled   if you want  i can even give you the authority as the leader  of course  on the surface  i ll make it look like i chose the participants  that way  we can compete as a group  can t we   i don t know much about your current friendships  it was a chance encounter  and i just let you choose randomly  if you re uncomfortable in the group  it would be hard to show your true abilities  right   anyway  i m glad the match seems to be happening  nagumo  it s a shame that third year students can t participate in the game directly   it s a rare opportunity involving ayanokoji  of course i want to meet his expectations   sorry  but i ll decline  that ticket price is soaked with the blood and sweat of the entire year  it s too heavy for me  who hasn t been involved  to accept  isn t it  she volunteered the leader role the moment she smelled the match  kiyotaka declines her authority offer  she declines nagumo s class a bet  she knows about the bet before anyone else  she challenges his presumption with cool disinterest  she wants him to shine  he sees through her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p60-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: She sniffed out the bet<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.60–62<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Break room; she strolls in late; she already knows about the Nagumo match and proposes handing over leader authority.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I&#x27;m sorry I&#x27;m late. Has the discussion been settled?”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If you want, I can even give you the authority as the leader. Of course, on the surface, I&#x27;ll make it look like I chose the participants. That way, we can compete as a group, can&#x27;t we?”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don&#x27;t know much about your current friendships. It was a chance encounter, and I just let you choose randomly. If you&#x27;re uncomfortable in the group, it would be hard to show your true abilities, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyway, I&#x27;m glad the match seems to be happening, Nagumo. It&#x27;s a shame that third-year students can&#x27;t participate in the game directly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It&#x27;s a rare opportunity involving Ayanokōji. Of course I want to meet his expectations.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry, but I&#x27;ll decline. That ticket price is soaked with the blood and sweat of the entire year. It&#x27;s too heavy for me, who hasn&#x27;t been involved, to accept, isn&#x27;t it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She volunteered the leader role the moment she smelled the match; Kiyotaka declines her authority offer; she declines Nagumo&#x27;s Class A-bet.<span class=\"pg\">p.60–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> She knows about the bet before anyone else; she challenges his presumption with cool disinterest.<span class=\"pg\">p.60–62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She wants him to shine; he sees through her.<span class=\"pg\">p.60–62<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p57-1\">← Before: Ch.2: The bet negotiation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.2: The leader lever<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p68-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"","w":"kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 2  the leader lever the telling hashimoto scene  she is named   i ll also try to extract as much information as possible at that time  but if kiryuin senpai doesn t make a move  your power is indispensable    his leverage phrase  she is the ceiling on what he can do  named in dialogue  not present on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: The leader lever<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.68<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The Telling Hashimoto scene; she is named.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “I&#x27;ll also try to extract as much information as possible at that time, but if Kiryūin-senpai doesn&#x27;t make a move, your power is indispensable.” — his leverage phrase; she is the ceiling on what he can do.<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Named in dialogue; not present on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p60-1\">← Before: Ch.2: She sniffed out the bet<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p71-1\">→ After: Ch.2: Between matches<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p71-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kouenji-rokusuke kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 2  between matches post oshibana in the workshop  she calls him over to talk tension and the match with nagumo   a victory s a good start  though  i didn t feel any tension   but if it s a competition based on experiential learning  it s not strange for anyone to win or lose   hashimoto made this list for me  which makes things easier  he s surprisingly useful   i m grateful for that  all i want to see is the match between you and nagumo  she lets inogashira approach with the koenji problem  she suggests trying to recruit him only if he wins for the private points  she takes no personal responsibility   there s still some time until the next game  why not give it a shot  from what i ve seen  tatebayashi s group is small and unlikely to win  but if koenji is competent  the situation might turn around somewhat  right   of course  the decision is up to you  regardless of the details  the fact that she came to us first is significant  she stays detached  only the match with nagumo interests her  she sees him as a lost cause unless money motivates him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p71-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: Between matches<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.71–73<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Post-oshibana in the workshop; she calls him over to talk tension and the match with Nagumo.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“A victory&#x27;s a good start. Though, I didn&#x27;t feel any tension.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“But if it&#x27;s a competition based on experiential learning, it&#x27;s not strange for anyone to win or lose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hashimoto made this list for me, which makes things easier. He&#x27;s surprisingly useful.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I&#x27;m grateful for that. All I want to see is the match between you and Nagumo.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She lets Inogashira approach with the Kōenji problem; she suggests trying to recruit him only if he wins for the private points; she takes no personal responsibility.<span class=\"pg\">p.72–73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There&#x27;s still some time until the next game, why not give it a shot? From what I&#x27;ve seen, Tatebayashi&#x27;s group is small and unlikely to win, but if Kōenji is competent, the situation might turn around somewhat. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course, the decision is up to you. Regardless of the details, the fact that she came to us first is significant.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She stays detached; only the match with Nagumo interests her.<span class=\"pg\">p.71–73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> She sees him as a lost cause unless money motivates him.<span class=\"pg\">p.72–73<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.2: The leader lever<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p79-1\">→ After: Ch.2: The swings<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p79-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"spoken","w":"asahina-nazuna ayanokouji-kiyotaka kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 2  the swings east park  she is on the swing with asahina  kiyotaka arrives to report koenji s refusal   are you that happy to talk to me   it s their law department  but i m not particularly attached to the department   hmm  i m not aiming for anything  i m not trying to become anything   i have a dream of not becoming anyone  does that answer your question   if i had to choose a job to achieve something  i might aim to be a politician   no  it was because of opportunities like that that i decided against becoming a politician  i just let their talk go in from one ear and out the other   because it s such a corrupt world  there are also those who shine  he was one of the few people i admired   it s kijima san  he s become quite important now   i don t plan to at the moment   didn t i tell you there s a lot going on   i see  since i m also aiming for the same path  we re both dream chasers in our own way  her dream  be a politician like kijima  now important   the prime minister  she admired him from childhood family ties  she refuses to aim for it because the kiryuin name follows her  asahina hangs on her every word about kijima and her future  she teases that he might become a politician  he declines  she is entertained by his defeat with koenji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p79-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: The swings<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.79–83<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">East park; she is on the swing with Asahina; Kiyotaka arrives to report Kōenji&#x27;s refusal.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"asahina-nazuna.html\">Asahina Nazuna<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Are you that happy to talk to me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It&#x27;s their law department. But I&#x27;m not particularly attached to the department.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hmm? I’m not aiming for anything. I’m not trying to become anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have a dream of not becoming anyone. Does that answer your question?”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I had to choose a job to achieve something, I might aim to be a politician.”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No? It was because of opportunities like that that I decided against becoming a politician. I just let their talk go in from one ear and out the other.”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because it&#x27;s such a corrupt world, there are also those who shine. He was one of the few people I admired.”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It&#x27;s Kijima-san. He&#x27;s become quite important now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don&#x27;t plan to at the moment.”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Didn&#x27;t I tell you there&#x27;s a lot going on?”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. Since I&#x27;m also aiming for the same path, we&#x27;re both dream chasers in our own way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her dream: be a politician like Kijima (now important / the Prime Minister); she admired him from childhood family ties; she refuses to aim for it because the Kiryūin name follows her.<span class=\"pg\">p.81–83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Asahina Nazuna<\/b> Asahina hangs on her every word about Kijima and her future.<span class=\"pg\">p.79–83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She teases that he might become a politician; he declines; she is entertained by his defeat with Kōenji.<span class=\"pg\">p.79–83<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p71-1\">← Before: Ch.2: Between matches<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p87-1\">→ After: Ch.3: The third-year context<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p87-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"","w":"kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 3  the third year context the sakayanagi verdict evening  she is named   if sakayanagi wanted to win  it would be normal for her to take command  regardless of whether it s a third year or whatever    she is one of the third year leaders named as comparison points  named in dialogue  not present on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p87-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: The third-year context<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.87<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The Sakayanagi verdict evening; she is named.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “If Sakayanagi wanted to win, it would be normal for her to take command, regardless of whether it&#x27;s a third-year or whatever.” — she is one of the third-year leaders named as comparison points.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Named in dialogue; not present on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p79-1\">← Before: Ch.2: The swings<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p108-1\">→ After: Ch.4: The breakfast table<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p108-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"","w":"kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 4  the breakfast table the breakfast  he is captivated   kiryuin  who had finished her meal early  leaned on the table and muttered with interest    she watches the first year frenzy  named in narration  on page from p 109","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: The breakfast table<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.108<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The breakfast; he is captivated.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Kiryūin, who had finished her meal early, leaned on the table and muttered with interest.” — she watches the first-year frenzy.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Named in narration; on-page from p.109.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p87-1\">← Before: Ch.3: The third-year context<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p109-1\">→ After: Ch.4: The third-year who won&#x27;t carry trays<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p109-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 4  the third year who won t carry trays breakfast  she finishes early  she probes the  magic  that tamed the first years   in less than a day  you ve tamed the first year students so well  what kind of magic did you use   do you intend to hide it from me too   hmm  a secret between men  that s not so bad   i appreciate the thought  but i can clean up after myself  let s meet again at the next exchange meeting  he blocks her probe with  a secret between men  she leaves oddly satisfied  she reads that he hides something from her too","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p109-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: The third-year who won&#x27;t carry trays<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.109<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Breakfast; she finishes early; she probes the “magic” that tamed the first-years.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“In less than a day, you&#x27;ve tamed the first-year students so well. What kind of magic did you use?”<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Do you intend to hide it from me too?”<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hmm, a secret between men. That&#x27;s not so bad.”<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I appreciate the thought, but I can clean up after myself. Let&#x27;s meet again at the next exchange meeting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> He blocks her probe with “a secret between men”; she leaves oddly satisfied.<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She reads that he hides something from her too.<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p108-1\">← Before: Ch.4: The breakfast table<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.5: The 16-game streak<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p116-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"","w":"kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 5  the 16 game streak the sculpture experience  she is named   even if the kiryuin group could win 16 or 17 games in a row by repeatedly buying off their opponents    kiyotaka s analysis  she is the presumed winner  named in narration  not present on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: The 16-game streak<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.116<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The sculpture experience; she is named.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Even if the Kiryūin group could win 16 or 17 games in a row by repeatedly buying off their opponents” — Kiyotaka&#x27;s analysis; she is the presumed winner.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Named in narration; not present on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p109-1\">← Before: Ch.4: The third-year who won&#x27;t carry trays<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p120-1\">→ After: Ch.5: The tied-for-sixth<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p120-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"","w":"kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 5  the tied for sixth the rest area  the rankings   kiryuin s group was tied for sixth place with nine wins and three losses  depending on tomorrow s results  it was possible to aim for the podium    the standings  her group is mid pack  named in narration  not present on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: The tied-for-sixth<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.120<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The rest area; the rankings.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Kiryūin&#x27;s group was tied for sixth place with nine wins and three losses. Depending on tomorrow&#x27;s results, it was possible to aim for the podium.” — the standings; her group is mid-pack.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Named in narration; not present on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p116-1\">← Before: Ch.5: The 16-game streak<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p135-1\">→ After: Ch.5: The girls&#x27; room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p135-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"","w":"kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 5  the girls  room the girls  room  she plays one liner foil to hashimoto   playing cards is the most classic of classics  isn t it  ayanokoji    her line  she sits and watches   isn t it suspicious to say you re confident in playing cards  that s why i left you out    her verdict on morishita  named in dialogue  not present in the card game itself","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p135-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: The girls&#x27; room<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.135–136<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The girls&#x27; room; she plays one-liner foil to Hashimoto.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Playing cards is the most classic of classics, isn&#x27;t it, Ayanokōji?” — her line; she sits and watches.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Isn&#x27;t it suspicious to say you&#x27;re confident in playing cards? That&#x27;s why I left you out.” — her verdict on Morishita.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Named in dialogue; not present in the card game itself.<span class=\"pg\">p.135–136<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p120-1\">← Before: Ch.5: The tied-for-sixth<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p152-1\">→ After: Ch.6: The shogi five<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p152-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"","w":"kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 6  the shogi five the shogi match lineup   the participants kiryuin chose were me  morishita  hashimoto  hiyori  and tsubaki    her five picks  she is the selector  named in narration  not present in the shogi five","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: The shogi five<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.152<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The shogi match lineup.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “The participants Kiryūin chose were me, Morishita, Hashimoto, Hiyori, and Tsubaki.” — her five picks; she is the selector.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Named in narration; not present in the shogi five.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p135-1\">← Before: Ch.5: The girls&#x27; room<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p156-1\">→ After: Ch.6: The forest wait<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p156-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"","w":"kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 6  the forest wait the forest scene  she is waiting at the building   morishita started walking away from under the tree    the walk back toward the inn  she is somewhere ahead of them  named in narration  not present in the forest scene","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p156-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: The forest wait<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.156<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The forest scene; she is waiting at the building.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Morishita started walking away from under the tree.” — the walk back toward the inn; she is somewhere ahead of them.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Named in narration; not present in the forest scene.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p152-1\">← Before: Ch.6: The shogi five<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p159-1\">→ After: Ch.6: The 17th match<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p159-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"","w":"kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 6  the 17th match the 17th match  her group loses one match   following a game of table tennis  the upcoming game was  archery  making it the second  archery  match in the exchange meeting    the matchup she selects   by the way  the only one who scored a total of six points and suffered a big loss in this game was morishita    her group wins four of five  she does not see it   kiryuin s group s final record was fifteen wins and four losses within the 19 games    the final record  her group finishes fourth  named in narration  not present in the match itself","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: The 17th match<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.159–162<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The 17th match; her group loses one match.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Following a game of table tennis, the upcoming game was &#x27;archery&#x27;, making it the second &#x27;archery&#x27; match in the exchange meeting.” — the matchup she selects.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “By the way, the only one who scored a total of six points and suffered a big loss in this game was Morishita.” — her group wins four of five; she does not see it.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Kiryūin&#x27;s group&#x27;s final record was fifteen wins and four losses within the 19 games.” — the final record; her group finishes fourth.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Mentioned<\/span> Named in narration; not present in the match itself.<span class=\"pg\">p.159–162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v11-p156-1\">← Before: Ch.6: The forest wait<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v12-p63-1","v":"y2v12","y":2,"o":31,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka nagumo-miyabi kiryuin-fuuka","q":"kiryuin fuuka ch 3  the bench before the exam 7 40 am  the school path  a student in casual clothes sitting on a bench   kiryuin senpai  a bag placed next to her  she was waiting for him before the exam   it s quite an early morning  what are you doing here  kiryuin senpai   i was waiting for you  i wanted to see you before you tackle the end of year special exam   it looks like you re about to leave   normally  third year students would ve already had their graduation ceremony and be out in the real world by now  she says she is busy looking for a new place to live  nagumo is curious how he will handle the exam but has no intention of seeing him  leaving the reconnaissance to her  she waves him off gently   she is looking forward to what he will produce   my apologies  concerned might be an overstatement   i m looking forward to seeing what results you ll bring about in the exam  third years have already had their graduation ceremony  she is a third year doing reconnaissance on nagumo s behalf  she speaks for nagumo  he is curious about the exam but refuses to see him himself","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kiryuin-fuuka-y2v12-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: The bench before the exam<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V12 · p.63–64<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">7:40 AM; the school path; a student in casual clothes sitting on a bench — Kiryūin-senpai; a bag placed next to her; she was waiting for him before the exam. She says she is busy looking for a new place to live; Nagumo is curious how he will handle the exam but has no intention of seeing him, leaving the reconnaissance to her; she waves him off gently — she is looking forward to what he will produce.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “It’s quite an early morning. What are you doing here, Kiryūin-senpai?”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I was waiting for you. I wanted to see you before you tackle the end-of-year special exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “It looks like you’re about to leave.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Normally, third-year students would’ve already had their graduation ceremony and be out in the real world by now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My apologies. Concerned might be an overstatement.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m looking forward to seeing what results you’ll bring about in the exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Third-years have already had their graduation ceremony; she is a third-year doing reconnaissance on Nagumo&#x27;s behalf.<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> She speaks for Nagumo; he is curious about the exam but refuses to see him himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"}];
